# MisakaX — Frontend UI (path-scoped)

Applies when editing **React components, pages, or stylesheet entry/tokens** under `src/` (`*.tsx`, `*.css`).

## Before coding

Read and comply with **every** spec that applies (they stack; do not pick one):

| Topic | File |
| ----- | ---- |
| Motion, color, desktop Agent tone | `docs/design/frontend-ui-guidelines.md` |
| Shell: nav vs session column, session toolbar, workspace bar | `docs/design/shell-and-workspace-ui-spec.md` |
| Buttons, menus, popovers, selects, dialogs, tooltips, toasts | `docs/design/button-menu-design-spec.md` |

Project stack and global expectations: root `CLAUDE.md` (Architecture, Code Style).

## After UI-facing work (mandatory wrap-up)

When the user asked to **change, adjust, polish, or refactor UI/UX** (layout, visuals, tokens, copy placement, interaction—not a pure non-visual logic tweak):

1. **Extract durable rules** — short, normative bullets (semantics, sizing, CSS variables, i18n/a11y). Omit one-off bug stories.
2. **Update `docs/design/`** — patch the smallest set of existing markdown specs; cross-link instead of pasting duplicates.
3. **Doc hygiene** — bump **“最后审阅 / Last reviewed”** (or equivalent) in any spec header you touched.

Do **not** wait for the user to ask for a separate documentation pass; treating spec updates as part of the same task is expected.
